[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> Host `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The threat actor exploited an exposed Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) endpoint configured with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following successful credential brute-forcing, the attacker established access, executed PowerShell scripts, deployed a ransomware payload, established three distinct persistence mechanisms (scheduled task, Windows service, registry Run key), and cleared the Windows Security event log to cover their tracks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Technical Attack Chain (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Step 1: Credential Access ‚Äî Brute Force (T1110)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Attacker conducted an automated RDP brute-force attack against the exposed RDP port (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Network-level exposure and NLA disabled configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Step 2: Lateral Movement / Initial Access ‚Äî Remote Desktop Protocol (T1021.001)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Attacker successfully logged in via RDP (Logon Type 10) from `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`, `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: CTI advisory log correlation (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`) and residual event log headers (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Step 3: Execution ‚Äî PowerShell (T1059.001)**
[?2004lWindows/Syste[?2004h>    - **Description**: Post-logon execution of malicious PowerShell commands to stage payloads and configure persistence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Threat advisory mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Step 4: Impact ‚Äî Data Encrypted for Impact / Ransomware (T1486)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Ransomware executable dropped at `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`. Appends `.locked` extension to encrypted files and drops ransom note (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Binary file on disk (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:3`).
[?2004l*Data[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Step 5: Execution / Persistence ‚Äî Scheduled Task (T1053.005)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Scheduled task named `UpdateHelper` created to run `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` every 5 minutes (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).
[?2004ldows/System32/svc-helper.s[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: On-disk task XML/file (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:11`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 6. **Step 6: Persistence ‚Äî Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder (T1547.001) [SILENT]**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Attacker added registry value `svc` under `HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run` referencing `C:\Users\Public\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Windows Registry SOFTWARE hive (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). **Note: This persistence mechanism was NOT flagged by EDR alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).**
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 7. **Step 7: Persistence ‚Äî Windows Service (T1543.003)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Malicious service `svc-helper` registered with binary at `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` configured to start at boot (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Service file on disk (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`), System Event Log EventID 7045 (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx:2`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:19`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 8. **Step 8: Defense Evasion ‚Äî Clear Windows Event Logs (T1070.001) [SILENT]**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Description**: Attacker cleared the Windows Security Event Log (`EventID 1102`) to impede investigation (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Security Event Log artifact (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`). **Note: This anti-forensic action was NOT flagged by EDR alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).**
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
