[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis & Software Flaw Assessment
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> A comprehensive analysis of vulnerability telemetry, system configuration, and threat intelligence was conducted to determine whether a software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited for initial entry into host `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Conclusion (Confidence Level: HIGH)**:
[?2004l[?2004h> **No software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited.** The attacker gained initial access purely via credential brute-forcing against Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`), facilitated by an insecure administrative configuration (`UserAuthentication = 0`, NLA disabled) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Analysis of Evidence
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Vulnerability Telemetry Feed (`/sas/vulns.json`)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The primary vulnerability scan output for host `rdp-prod-01` is empty `[]` (`/sas/vulns.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - No active CVEs, unpatched software vulnerabilities, or unauthenticated remote code execution flaws were identified on the host prior to or during the compromise.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Reconciling Initial Shift Hypotheses (CVE-2019-0708 / BlueKeep)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - In draft ticket `CHG-9792`, the prior shift suggested patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Rejection**: CVE-2019-0708 affects legacy Windows RDP protocol stacks. The target host runs Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`), which is not vulnerable to CVE-2019-0708.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Threat intelligence advisory confirms the campaign initial access vector was brute force (ATT&CK T1110) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`), not vulnerability exploitation.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **True Vector: Weak Configuration vs. Software Vulnerability**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The initial access was purely configuration-driven.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Network Level Authentication (NLA) was disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`) in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - NLA disabling allows unauthenticated RDP protocol handshakes, enabling offline/online password brute-forcing directly against the Windows logon interface without requiring prior authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary Table
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Category | Finding | CVE / Flaw ID | Confidence | Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Software Vulnerabilities | None Identified | N/A | HIGH | `/sas/vulns.json:1` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Proposed Remediation Row 2 | Incorrect BlueKeep claim | CVE-2019-0708 (Invalid) | HIGH | `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Primary Entry Vector | Weak Auth / Misconfiguration | N/A (T1110 Brute Force) | HIGH | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@3fe891a2496e:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline & Configuration Weakness Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## System Baseline Assessment
[?2004l[?2004h> An evaluation of baseline configurations and security controls on `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) revealed several critical configuration defects that facilitated initial access, enabled brute-force exploitation, and reduced forensic visibility.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Baseline Defects
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Disabled Network Level Authentication (NLA) for Remote Desktop Protocol
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding ID**: `CHK-06` / `BAS-01` (`/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Registry Path**: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` 
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Current State**: `UserAuthentication = 0` (NLA Disabled, connections allowed).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Security Impact**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Disabling NLA permits unauthenticated clients to initiate full TLS/RDP handshakes and render the Windows logon interface before authenticating.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - This exposes the host to remote credential brute-forcing (ATT&CK T1110) without triggering pre-authentication kerberos/NLA checks or network-level blocking (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Recommended Baseline Standard**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Enforce `UserAuthentication = 1` (`fPromptForPassword = 1`, `UserAuthentication = 1`) via Group Policy (`HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server\WinStations\RDP-Tcp`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Direct Exposure of RDP Service to Untrusted Public Networks
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding ID**: Network exposure baseline failure (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Context**: RDP port (3389) accessible directly from public internet IP addresses including attacker source `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Security Impact**: Directly exposing RDP port 3389 without access control lists (ACLs), VPN requirements, or IP whitelisting allows continuous brute-force attempts from external threat actors.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Recommended Baseline Standard**: Restrict RDP access to management VPN ranges or administrative bastion hosts via Host Firewall and Network Security Groups.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Inadequate Local Event Log Tamper Resistance & Central Log Forwarding
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding ID**: Anti-forensic log clearance vulnerability (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Context**: Security event logs were stored solely locally on disk without real-time forwarding to a remote SIEM or syslog server (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Security Impact**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - The attacker was able to clear the Security Event Log (`EventID 1102`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Because log forwarding was not configured, clearing local event logs destroyed the audit trail of process execution, user privileges, and command-line activity.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Recommended Baseline Standard**: Enable Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) or agent-based log streaming to an isolated remote SIEM server with append-only access controls.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Compliance Summary Table
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Control ID | Configuration Check | Standard Baseline | Current Non-Compliant State | Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | BAS-01 (CHK-06) | RDP Network Level Authentication | NLA Required (`UserAuthentication=1`) | NLA Disabled (`UserAuthentication=0`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | BAS-02 | RDP Perimeter Security | Restricted to VPN / Bastion | Open to Public Internet (`198.51.100.92`) | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | BAS-03 | Audit Log Retention | Remote Forwarding (SIEM) | Local-only, Cleared (EventID 1102) | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@3fe891a2496e:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
